FFmpeg
------
Beacon bundles FFmpeg 7.1.3 (https://ffmpeg.org): the ffmpeg and ffprobe
command-line tools and the shared libraries libavformat, libavcodec,
libavfilter, libavutil, libswscale and libswresample, which Beacon's engine
links dynamically. Beacon's build of FFmpeg contains no GPL or non-free parts
(it is configured without --enable-gpl, --enable-version3 and
--enable-nonfree), so it is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public
License (LGPL) version 2.1 or later:
https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.html

It is built by scripts/build-tools.ts from the unmodified release source
(https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-7.1.3.tar.xz, SHA-256
f0bf043299db9e3caacb435a712fc541fbb07df613c4b893e8b77e67baf3adbe) with one
change to its configure script, which adds the line
    enabled metadata_filter     && prepend avfilter_deps "avformat"
after the matching fsync_filter line, and with the configure options listed
in that script. The source, the change and the options are attached to every
Beacon release. You may replace the bundled FFmpeg libraries in
Beacon.app/Contents/Resources/app/engine with your own compatible build.

FFmpeg is linked with libvpx 1.15.2 (https://chromium.googlesource.com/webm/libvpx,
Copyright (c) 2010, The WebM Project authors, BSD 3-Clause License) and
Opus 1.5.2 (https://opus-codec.org, Copyright 2001-2023 Xiph.Org, Skype
Limited, Octasic, Jean-Marc Valin, Timothy B. Terriberry, CSIRO, Gregory
Maxwell, Mark Borgerding, Erik de Castro Lopo, Mozilla, Amazon, BSD 3-Clause
License), both built statically from their release sources, and with LAME
3.100 (https://lame.sourceforge.io, Copyright 1999-2017 The LAME Project,
Mike Cheng, Mark Taylor and others), for MP3 export, built statically from its
unmodified release source
(https://downloads.sourceforge.net/project/lame/lame/3.100/lame-3.100.tar.gz,
SHA-256 ddfe36cab873794038ae2c1210557ad34857a4b6bdc515785d1da9e175b1da1e)
into libavcodec. LAME is licensed under the GNU Library General Public License
version 2 or later (https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.0.html);
its source is attached to every Beacon release with FFmpeg's, and replacing
the bundled libavcodec replaces it.

